

This lab focuses on the basic configuration of two Cisco switches connected to four PCs.

The purpose of the lab is to practice essential Cisco IOS commands and basic LAN configuration.

Topology

PC1 ─── SW1 ───── SW2 ─── PC3
PC2 ───┘          └────── PC4

Devices

- 2 × Cisco Switches
- 4 × PCs

Configuration Tasks

The following basic configurations were performed on both switches:

- Hostname
- Enable secret
- Console line password
- VTY line password
- VLAN 1 management IP address
- Interface activation

IP Addressing

Device| IP Address| Subnet Mask
SW1| 192.168.1.2| 255.255.255.0
SW2| 192.168.1.3| 255.255.255.0
PC1| 192.168.1.10| 255.255.255.0
PC2| 192.168.1.11| 255.255.255.0
PC3| 192.168.1.12| 255.255.255.0
PC4| 192.168.1.13| 255.255.255.0

Verification

The following commands were used to verify the switch configuration:

show running-config
show ip interface brief

Connectivity between the PCs was verified using:

ping

Skills Demonstrated

- Basic Cisco IOS configuration
- Switch hostname configuration
- Console and VTY configuration
- Management IP addressing
- Basic LAN connectivity
- Network verification and troubleshooting
